Built-in "Blink" program (src/mcu/programs/blink.ts)
----------------------------------------------------

The Intel HEX data in src/mcu/programs/blink.ts (BLINK_HEX) is the compiled
form of src/mcu/programs/blink.c, which is original Gatehouse code. It was
built with WinAVR 20100110 (avr-gcc 4.3.3, avr-libc 1.6.7):

    avr-gcc -mmcu=atmega328p -Os -DF_CPU=16000000UL -o blink.elf blink.c
    avr-objcopy -O ihex -R .eeprom blink.elf blink.hex

The linker adds standard start-up code to every such program, so the hex
also contains compiled code that is not ours (checked with the linker map):

  - crtm328p.o from avr-libc: the interrupt vector table and the start-up
    code that sets up the stack and calls main(). Licence: the avr-libc
    licence below.
  - _copy_data.o, _clear_bss.o and _exit.o from GCC's libgcc.a (avr5):
    copying initialised data to RAM, clearing .bss, and the stop loop after
    main() returns. See "GCC runtime library (libgcc)" below.

Gatehouse ships this hex in its built JavaScript, so the notices below go
with every copy of the built app (the web build and the Electron app).


