WebAssembly AVR toolchain (development and browser compiler)
=============================================================

What this covers
----------------

Gatehouse compiles Arduino sketches with the GNU AVR toolchain built as
WebAssembly by the project https://github.com/startabit/avr-gcc-wasm (release
v1, built from commit 6972a73, published under GPL-3.0). The files are
downloaded, never committed to this repository (npm run toolchain:fetch puts
them in toolchain/, which is git-ignored). Every copy of Gatehouse that
includes or downloads these files (the web build's compiler packs and the
Electron app's resources) is covered by this section, and the licence texts in
licenses/toolchain/ (dist/licenses/ in the built app) go with it.

The files are:

  - four programs, each a .wasm module with its Emscripten JavaScript glue
    (.mjs): cc1plus (the C++ compiler), as (assembler), ld (linker) and
    objcopy (hex converter);
  - a "sysroot": GCC and avr-libc header files, the start-up code and
    libraries for the ATmega328P (crtatmega328p.o, libc.a, libm.a, libgcc.a,
    libatmega328p.a), the linker scripts (ldscripts/avr5.*), and the Arduino
    AVR core and libraries as precompiled archives with their headers
    (core.a, Wire, SPI, SoftwareSerial, EEPROM, Servo, Adafruit NeoPixel,
    HC-SR04).

